// Flashback = two statics [CR#702.34a]: a graveyard cast permission at an
// alternative cost ([CR#118.9] territory), tagged `Flashback` so a rider can
// ask "was this cast that way", and an exile-instead replacement gated on
// that tag via `Conditionally(CastWith(Flashback), …)`. The exile half is
// factored into the shared static/ExileWhenLeavesStack macro (reused by the
// other graveyard-recast keywords). The cast half is left inline by CHOICE,
// not by limitation: the macro layer CAN forward a `Param` into a nested
// macro invocation (see `PowerAndToughnessUp`, and the `macro-param-
// forwarding` machinery — a factored `CastFromGraveyard(Param(0))` expands
// fine). Factoring the cast half into its own `StaticEffect`-kind macro would
// only wrap every Flashback card's permission in an extra remembered-
// `Expanded` layer with no rendering gain, so it is deferred to a
// graveyard-recast-family factoring pass rather than done here.
// CAVEAT: the "was cast this way" linkage now lands in the SHAPE via the
// `tag`/`Conditionally(CastWith(Flashback), …)` pair, so the exile row no
// longer over-claims on paper. Engine GATING of a `Conditionally` static is
// still a currently-unwired seam (see `StaticEffect::Conditionally`'s own
// doc, [CR#611.3a]) — runtime firing lands with `engine-alt-costs`. The
// shape is correct and round-trips today.
(
    name: "Flashback",
    template: "flashback ${0}",
    kinds: [KeywordAbility],
    params: [Cost],
    body: Composite(
        name: "Flashback",
        abilities: [
            Static(May(Cast(what: Ref(This), from: Graveyard, cost: Components(Param(0)), tag: Flashback))),
            Static(Conditionally(CastWith(Flashback), ExileWhenLeavesStack)),
        ],
    ),
)
